==English==
===Etymology===
From {{etyl|hwc}} [[w:craps|craps]] slang, meaning “to wager everything on one roll”: one would be [[broke]], [[bankrupt]] if one loses.<ref>The movie [[w:Go for Broke! (1951 film)|Go for Broke!]], which popularized this phrase, gives this etymology.</ref>

Popularized by the movie [[w:Go for Broke! (1951 film)|Go for Broke!]] (1951), which is named for the [[w:442nd Infantry Regiment (United States)|442nd Infantry Regiment’s]] [[w:Military Unit Mottos: United States|unit motto]].

===Verb===
'''[[go]] for [[broke]]'''
#To [[wager]] everything.
#{{idiom}} To try everything possible or do last thing possible in a final attempt.

